   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF humanitarian action in Ethiopia, 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response to a humanitarian appeal; results framework not included.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This allocation of 15 mio. DKK contributes to the objectives of UNICEF&#x2019;s humanitarian response in Ethiopia. Key planned results for 2023 include: 1.2 million children admitted for treatment for severe acute malnutrition, 2.1 million children and women accessing primary healthcare, 7.3 million children using safe and appropriate WASH services, 275,012 children/caregivers accessing mental health and psychosocial support.
&#x2022;	187,000 children/caregivers accessing mental health and psychosocial support</narrative>
